flags={}; failed={}
def add(n, checks, text):
 i=f'W11-L53-Q{n:03}';flags.setdefault(i,[]).append(text);failed.setdefault(i,set()).update(checks.split())
add(4,'distractors','Replace the conspicuous zero-current force alternative o4 and whole-wire/carrier equal-speed claim o3 with physically credible alternatives that distinguish carrier drift, bulk translation and induced EMF. The key and source qualification are correct; these alternatives are not competitive misconceptions at the same level.')
add(5,'sourceSupport','The sole citation is the perpendicular special case F=BIL on page 1689, but the question requires sin(30°). Add the actual cross-product premise on page 1688 with its exact locator, retaining the declared straight-wire angle and length assumptions.')
add(6,'distractors','Option o1 says the magnetic field must first be switched off, an unrelated condition rather than a plausible motional-EMF error. Replace it with a credible velocity/field/rod projection or open-circuit-versus-current misconception; preserve the explicit added vector model.')
add(11,'distractors','Options o1 (eliminate the field throughout rotation) and o2 (keep current unchanged despite stated reversal) are too readily rejected without understanding commutation. Use competing torque-sense/current-switching phase interpretations of the actual loop sequence.')
for n in [17,18]:add(n,'sourceSupport explanation','The tested and cited law is V_b=K_vω on page 1693, but the formula record imports the entire armature R/L circuit and steady torque-speed law without page 1694 support. Narrow this record to back EMF with its units, or add exact source premises for every retained law; avoid an unrelated omnibus formula.')
add(22,'distractors','All three alternatives assert no-load stall, zero back EMF or stall-level current. Replace at least the conspicuous no-load-equals-stall choices with plausible distinctions among external load torque, internal friction/iron losses, electromagnetic torque and armature current.')
add(30,'distractors','The high-no-load-speed stem rules out o1 zero speed and o2 stall speed almost verbatim. Use credible series-motor flux/current/load or rated-speed protection mistakes rather than these self-contradictory alternatives.')
add(32,'sourceSupport explanation','Add page 1694 for the armature back-EMF voltage balance used in the solution; page 1696 supports the qualified shunt topology but not the complete R/L/torque-speed formula imported here. Prefer the narrowly tested I_a=(V−V_b)/R_a, I_f=V/R_f and line-current sum with exact premises.')
add(33,'distractors','Option o4 reverses field polarity whenever load rises, unrelated to ordinary shunt regulation. Replace it with a credible confusion about armature resistive drop, field strength or current/load coupling. The approximate-regulation qualification and cited equations are correct.')
add(34,'sourceSupport explanation','The cited pages 1693/1696 support fixed-flux T=K_t I_a and the conflicting sketch, but the formula record adds an uncited full R/L circuit and torque-speed law. Narrow the metadata to the tested direct proportionality, or cite page 1694 explicitly for retained circuit relations.')
add(36,'distractors','Option o1 calls all these explicitly wound-field motors permanent-magnet types. Replace it with a credible alternate shunt/series/compound resistance mapping, parallel to the other table-based choices.')
add(43,'sourceSupport','Page 1699 contains the claim being qualified, not the electrical and mechanical relations that justify the answer. Add page 1693/1694 for torque/back EMF/circuit and page 1710 for load balance, using exact premise roles and locators.')
add(43,'distractors','Option o4 says current determines only rotor position and has no torque relation; replace it with a plausible partial electrical/load constraint rather than an unrelated position claim.')
add(46,'distractors','Options o2 permanent rail short in every state and o3 position determination are implausible diode functions. Use credible current-continuity, clamping-polarity or stored-energy alternatives, or replace this recall item with the bounded bridge current-path exercise in the coverage challenge.')
add(50,'distractors explanation','Option o3=5 rad/s has no specified credible error mechanism; its explanation merely says it is not the calibrated difference. Replace it with a reproducible calibration/gain/sign error and explain the exact arithmetic leading to that alternative.')
add(51,'distractors','Encoder-removes-inertia and ADC-infinite-bandwidth alternatives are conspicuous nonphysical claims. Retain the important stability qualification but use realistic gain, sampling/delay and plant-dynamics alternatives.')
add(53,'distractors','The three-external-optical-encoder and fewer-sensors-implies-brushed-armature alternatives conflate unrelated construction choices. Replace them with plausible Hall/commutation/sensorless-estimation distinctions; keep item-bound TI evidence and the correct qualified answer.')
for n in [55,60]:add(n,'sourceSupport explanation','This synchronous-speed task imports induction slip and rotor speed in its formula record although neither is tested or supported by the cited synchronous/pole-count premises. Narrow to n_s=60f/p=120f/P with variables and units. Retain slip only on an explicitly qualified, supported slip exercise.')
add(57,'distractors','Option o4 excludes electromagnetic torque from every AC motor, an unrelated conspicuous falsehood. Replace it with a plausible distinction among induced rotor current, permanent-magnet rotor field and external field excitation; retain the heading-specific qualification.')
add(61,'sourceSupport assumptions','The pre-answer assumptions say an added standard slip definition exists, but do not actually give it; neither cited page prints s=(n_s−n_r)/n_s. Supply the actual added definition in the stem/assumptions or bind an appropriate explicitly supplemental primary premise, rather than presenting an unexplained outside formula as slide recall. The 1500 rpm/4% key and alternatives are numerically correct.')
add(63,'distractors','Option o2 equates physical phase count with a pulse rate and rotor teeth with command count, while o1 adds unrelated heating. Replace these with plausible count/rate/step-angle or timing confusions in a parallel form.')
for n in [64,65,66]:add(n,'sourceSupport explanation','The full-step task cites page 1707 but its generic formula record introduces microstep factor m absent from that cited page. Narrow to the tested full-step relations with m=1, or explicitly cite page 1712 for retained microstepping premises and mark its nominal/no-missed-step scope.')
add(65,'difficulty','This is two direct specified count/angle and count/rate conversions, with no coupled inference or uncertainty. Label easy, consistent with adjacent step-count and speed items, unless the task is substantively enriched rather than relabeled.')
add(66,'explanation','The o3=100000 rpm explanation names multiplication by steps/revolution but omits the additional failure to convert seconds to minutes. Explain both errors explicitly or replace the value with one produced by the precise stated error model.')
add(78,'distractors','Option o3 claims inertia prohibits acceleration. Replace this conspicuous nonphysical alternative with a credible distinction involving net torque, damping/slope or a neutral operating point while preserving the source-specific stable sign pattern.')
add(84,'distractors','All three alternatives erase waveform distinctions or deny applications explicitly supplied in the same stem/source. Use competing plausible scope statements about application class, historical prevalence and drive/system terminology, rather than universal absences that give away the only qualified answer.')
add(87,'sourceSupport explanation','The only citation, page 1709, supports duty-cycle selection but not T=K_t I or copper-loss electrical premises. Add exact page 1693/1694 premises and narrow formula metadata to I_j=T_j/K_t, I_j²R and the time-weighted average. The 24 W key and all three numerical alternatives are independently correct.')
add(88,'sourceSupport explanation assumptions','The correct two-case flux-scaling solution is accompanied by an omnibus uncited R/L/steady torque-speed record and an unqualified constant-flux assumption. Narrow to the declared parameter scaling plus ω_0=V/K_v and I=T/K_t, explaining that each case has constant flux internally but flux differs between cases. Add page 1694 if retaining its circuit relation. Do not change the correct both-double answer or collapse the two distinct operating comparisons.')
